# November 6 evidence update; original historical manuscript remains unchanged.
new=[]
def NP(t): new.append(('p',t))
new.append(('h','5.5. Protected projections and paired-board training'))
NP('Trial 024 fitted a rank-two color span using 63 training boards and checked it on 65 other boards from the same training inventory. A direct edit removed the constant positional contribution orthogonal to that span, changing 1,152 weights without gradient updates. Check-set occupancy NLL improved from 0.1701690 to 0.1683686 (1.058%), while teacher-forced exact answers fell from 39/65 to 38/65. All six normal development conditions generated 32/48 correct answers. Geometric protection of a fitted span therefore did not establish behavioral preservation. Reverse, random, shrink and full-mean controls were retained; 017 remained the reference.')
NP('Passive capture 025 and CPU recovery 026 examined the learned path on 128 training boards. Queried-square attention was correct on 83/128, sender queried-cell occupancy on 90/128, and both on only 58/128. Own stones were reconstructed as opponent stones on 23 of 42 queried own-stone examples. A simple linear probe became less accurate after the value/output map, but the map had full column rank and an approximate inverse recovered the original value-probe predictions. Reduced linear-probe performance was therefore not evidence that the map destroyed color information. These are reused-training diagnostics, not autonomous task gains.')
NP('Trial 027 changed only receiver value and output projections from 017. It used 60 same-square, different-label training pairs plus replay, optimizing native answer CE and a paired log-odds hinge with weight 0.25 and margin 2. Across three epochs it retained 180 updates and 720 repeated prompt exposures over 189 unique rows; four qualification updates were discarded. Training took 84.89 seconds (8.48 exposures/s). Mean hinge fell from 1.6354 to 0.33125 and CE from 0.25124 to 0.17115. This combined-objective experiment does not isolate the hinge as the cause of any outcome.')
new.append(('table','Table 5. Actual generated answers for 017 and paired-board receiver 027 on the reused panel. Legal moves and preferred-move matches are different metrics.',['Measure','017','027'],[['Occupancy /16','8','9'],['Capture /16','11','7'],['Legality /16','9','9'],['Liberties /16','10','10'],['Preferred expert move /16','0','1'],['Legal moves /16','10','3'],['Arithmetic /16','16','16'],['All generated answers /96','54','52']]))
